{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.no_constant_surface_coefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.no_constant_surface_coefficient","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.lean#L75-L90","doc":"**The exclusion.** No single constant `c` makes the affine count equal a\nsurface term at two distinct positive mass numbers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.ratio_strictMono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.ratio_strictMono","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**The ratio is strictly monotone on the positives.** Both `12 * m` and\n`-m⁻²` increase, so their sum does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.ratio_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.ratio_eq","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.lean#L58-L62","doc":"On `m > 0` the ratio really is count / surface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.ratio","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The ratio of the count to a surface term, in the cube variable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.surfaceOfCube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.surfaceOfCube","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.lean#L52-L53","doc":"A surface term in the cube variable: `A ^ (2/3) = m ^ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.countOfCube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.countOfCube","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.lean#L49-L50","doc":"The crossing count in the cube variable: `A = m ^ 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.crossingCount_eq_four_mul_strands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.crossingCount_eq_four_mul_strands","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.lean#L44-L47","doc":"`n_strands = 3 * A`, so the count is `4 * n_strands - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.crossingCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.crossingCount","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCountIsNotASurfaceTerm.lean#L41-L42","doc":"The measured canonical-braid crossing count, as a function of mass number. ","signatureChunk":0}]}